\",[\"$\",\"$L14\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/reference/visual-editor\",\"children\":\"visual editor reference\"}],\" for guidance on using the visual editor.\"]}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"note relative mt-4 rounded border border-solid border-[#86efac] bg-[#f0fdf4] pb-2 pl-9 pr-3 pt-3 text-base leading-normal tracking-tight md:text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute left-3 top-3 inline-block h-[18px] w-[18px] text-[#15803d]\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":\"18px\",\"height\":\"18px\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":\"2\",\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14\"}],[\"$\",\"polyline\",null,{\"points\":\"22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01\"}]]}]}],[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"You can also reference groups of Tailscale Services using a tag you've assigned to each Service. This example grants access to a group of production Services with access to the Service \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"svc:database\"}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"group relative overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute right-[5px] top-[21px] flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded bg-gray-200 text-gray-1000 opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L19\",null,{\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"src\\\":  [\\\"tag:prod-service\\\"],\\n  \\\"dst\\\":  [\\\"svc:database\\\"],\\n  \\\"ip\\\": [\\\"5432\\\"],\\n},\\n\"}]}],[\"$\",\"pre\",null,{\"className\":\"refractor language-json\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"language-json\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-0\",{\"className\":\"token punctuation\",\"children\":[\"{\"]}],\"\\n  \",[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-2\",{\"className\":\"token property\",\"children\":[\"\\\"src\\\"\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-3\",{\"className\":\"token operator\",\"children\":[\":\"]}],\"  \",[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-5\",{\"className\":\"token punctuation\",\"children\":[\"[\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-6\",{\"className\":\"token string\",\"children\":[\"\\\"tag:prod-service\\\"\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-7\",{\"className\":\"token punctuation\",\"children\":[\"]\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-8\",{\"className\":\"token punctuation\",\"children\":[\",\"]}],\"\\n  \",[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-10\",{\"className\":\"token property\",\"children\":[\"\\\"dst\\\"\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-11\",{\"className\":\"token operator\",\"children\":[\":\"]}],\"  \",[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-13\",{\"className\":\"token punctuation\",\"children\":[\"[\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-14\",{\"className\":\"token string\",\"children\":[\"\\\"svc:database\\\"\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-15\",{\"className\":\"token punctuation\",\"children\":[\"]\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-16\",{\"className\":\"token punctuation\",\"children\":[\",\"]}],\"\\n  \",[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-18\",{\"className\":\"token property\",\"children\":[\"\\\"ip\\\"\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-19\",{\"className\":\"token operator\",\"children\":[\":\"]}],\" \",[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-21\",{\"className\":\"token punctuation\",\"children\":[\"[\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-22\",{\"className\":\"token string\",\"children\":[\"\\\"5432\\\"\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-23\",{\"className\":\"token punctuation\",\"children\":[\"]\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-24\",{\"className\":\"token punctuation\",\"children\":[\",\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-26\",{\"className\":\"token punctuation\",\"children\":[\"}\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-27\",{\"className\":\"token punctuation\",\"children\":[\",\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]}]]}]]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"id\":\"use-access-control-tests\",\"children\":\"Use access control tests\",\"level\":3}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Tailscale Services resources are valid \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"accept\"}],\" or \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"deny\"}],\" destinations in \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/reference/syntax/policy-file#tests\",\"children\":\"access control tests\"}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"id\":\"check-availability\",\"children\":\"Check availability\",\"level\":3}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"To check the availability of your Service, you can use the \",[\"$\",\"$L14\",null,{\"href\":\"https://console.tailscale.com/admin/services\",\"className\":\"!font-bold !text-[#3b82f6] underline decoration-blue-50 underline-offset-4 hover:!text-[#2563eb] hover:!decoration-[#3b82f6] focus-visible:no-underline\",\"children\":\"Services\"}],\" page of the admin console.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"Open the \",[\"$\",\"$L14\",null,{\"href\":\"https://console.tailscale.com/admin/services\",\"className\":\"!font-bold !text-[#3b82f6] underline decoration-blue-50 underline-offset-4 hover:!text-[#2563eb] hover:!decoration-[#3b82f6] focus-visible:no-underline\",\"children\":\"Services\"}],\" page of the Tailscale admin console.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"Within the \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Advertised\"}],\" section, you should find your Tailscale Service listed with configured endpoints.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"id\":\"reference\",\"children\":\"Reference\",\"level\":2}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"This section provides reference information about Tailscale Services, including endpoint types and service states.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"id\":\"endpoint-types\",\"children\":\"Endpoint types\",\"level\":3}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Tailscale supports three types of endpoints, each operating at different layers of the networking stack. While the OSI model isn't a perfect representation of modern networking, it provides a useful framework for understanding these distinctions. There are three different types of endpoints: layer 7 (application), layer 4 (transport), and layer 3 (network). This section explains each type, when to use them, and notes about their specific capabilities\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"id\":\"layer-7-endpoints-application-layer\",\"children\":\"Layer 7 endpoints (application layer)\",\"level\":4}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Layer 7 (application) endpoints provide the most sophisticated forwarding mechanism by understanding and manipulating application layer protocols. It can inspect, modify, and route traffic based on application-specific content. These types of endpoints work well when you need Tailscale to inject authentication headers in the packets or path-based routing. For example, \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"/api/*\"}],\" requests might go to one server while \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"/static/*\"}],\" goes to another.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"You can create a layer 7 endpoint by setting the protocol value to \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"http\"}],\" or \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"https\"}],\" when using \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tailscale serve\"}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"The port number is the port to expose the endpoint on.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"You can use the optional \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"--set-path\"}],\" flag to use a custom file path. By default, it uses \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"/\"}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"The destination can be text, a file path, or a local address. Refer to \",[\"$\",\"$L14\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/reference/examples/serve\",\"children\":\"Tailscale Serve examples\"}],\" for more examples.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"id\":\"layer-4-endpoints-transport-layer\",\"children\":\"Layer 4 endpoints (transport layer)\",\"level\":4}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Layer 4 (transport) endpoints operate at the transport (TCP) layer of the \",[\"$\",\"$L14\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/concepts/tailscale-osi\",\"children\":\"OSI model\"}],\". They act as TCP forwarders that don't modify packet data, but might not preserve packet boundaries and metadata. These types of endpoints work well for standard TCP services like web servers and databases. They have less overhead than layer 7 endpoints because they don't parse application layer protocols.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"You can create a layer 4 endpoint by setting the protocol value to \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tcp\"}],\" or \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tls-terminated-tcp\"}],\" when using \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tailscale serve\"}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"The port number is the port to expose a TCP forwarder on. The TCP forwarder forwards raw TLS-terminated packets.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"You cannot use the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"--set-path\"}],\" flag to use a custom file path. It must be empty or unset.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"The destination is the local address where the raw TCP packets will be forwarded to (for example, \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tcp://localhost:5432\"}],\").\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"id\":\"layer-3-endpoints-network-layer\",\"children\":\"Layer 3 endpoints (network layer)\",\"level\":4}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Layer 3 (network) endpoints are a special type of endpoint that operates at the IP packet level and forwards all traffic, unmodified, to the operating system networking stack.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"You might consider using a layer 3 endpoint if the application or resource you're serving requires UDP support or you need to preserve exact packet boundaries and sizes. However, keep in mind that they have the following limitations:\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Require additional operating system configuration to handle the unmodified packets.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Don't have any built-in application layer features like authentication headers.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":\"Only work on Linux.\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"You can create a layer 3 endpoint on a Linux device by running the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tailscale serve\"}],\" command (with the service information) with the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"--tun\"}],\" flag.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"group relative overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute right-[5px] top-[21px] flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded bg-gray-200 text-gray-1000 opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L19\",null,{\"text\":\"tailscale serve --service=svc:\u003cservice-name\u003e --tun\\n\"}]}],[\"$\",\"pre\",null,{\"className\":\"refractor language-shell\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"language-shell\",\"children\":[\"tailscale serve --service\",[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-1\",{\"className\":\"token operator\",\"children\":[\"=\"]}],\"svc:\",[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-3\",{\"className\":\"token operator\",\"children\":[\"\u003c\"]}],\"service-name\",[\"$\",\"span\",\"fract-0-5\",{\"className\":\"token operator\",\"children\":[\"\u003e\"]}],\" --tun\\n\"]}]}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Using the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"--tun\"}],\" flag creates a layer 3 protocol-agnostic endpoint, which offers more control over the way packets flow to the resource. This type of endpoint forwards all traffic heading to the Tailscale Service to your local device without modifying it. In this mode, you would likely be doing some of your own \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"iptables\"}],\" configuration or something like that to take full control of the packet and make it go to your desired destination.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"id\":\"service-states\",\"children\":\"Service states\",\"level\":3}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"This section covers the states of Services in the admin console. In the Services page of the admin console, a Service can be in the following states:\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Pending approval\"}],\": The Service has one or more hosts that have been advertised but are awaiting approval from an \",[\"$\",\"$L14\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/reference/user-roles/\",\"className\":\"!font-medium !text-[#3b82f6] underline decoration-blue-50 underline-offset-4 hover:!text-[#2563eb] hover:!decoration-[#3b82f6] focus-visible:no-underline\",\"children\":\"Admin, Network admin, or Owner\"}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Needs configuration\"}],\": The host has been defined but has an invalid or missing configuration.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Connected\"}],\": At least one host is actively advertising the Service.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Offline\"}],\": No hosts are currently advertising the Service.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Pre-approved\"}],\": A device has been automatically approved based on an auto-approval policy but is not yet advertising the Service.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Draining\"}],\": The host is in the process of draining, meaning it is no longer accepting new connections but is still handling existing ones.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"id\":\"limitations\",\"children\":\"Limitations\",\"level\":2}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Tailscale Services has the following limitations:\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"TCP-only protocol support\"}],\": Services currently only support TCP transport protocol, with UDP unavailable except through layer 3 endpoints on Linux that require additional operating system (OS) level configuration.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"No outgoing connections\"}],\": Virtual IP addresses (TailVIPs) assigned to Services can only accept incoming connections, preventing any outgoing connections from being initiated.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Linux-only layer 3 endpoints\"}],\": Layer 3 endpoints that preserve packet boundaries only work on Linux and require additional tool configuration, such as \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"iptables\"}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Text and file endpoints\"}],\": The Service configuration file method does not support \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"text:\"}],\" or \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"file:\"}],\" destinations. These are only available when using the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tailscale serve\"}],\" CLI command.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Limitations with multiple network interfaces\"}],\": Service Hosts that have multiple network interfaces and define remote resource destinations might experience issues in specific circumstances. For example, a connection to a remote destination might fail if:\",\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"The Service Host (1) is a Linux device, (2) is running \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tailscaled\"}],\" without \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"SO_MARK\"}],\", (3) has multiple network interfaces, and (4) does not have the remote destination in its default route table. You can bypass this limitation by running \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tailscaled\"}],\" in \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/reference/kernel-vs-userspace-routers#userspace-netstack-mode\",\"children\":\"userspace-networking mode\"}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"The Service Host (1) is a macOS device using the \",[\"$\",\"$L14\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/concepts/macos-variants\",\"children\":\"Mac App Store or Standalone variant\"}],\", (2) has multiple network interfaces, and (3) does not have the remote endpoint in its default route table. In this case, you can bypass the issue by running the \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/concepts/macos-variants#open-source-tailscaled-variant\",\"children\":\"open source macOS variant\"}],\" (which uses \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tailscaled\"}],\" in userspace-networking mode by default).\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"id\":\"additional-information\",\"children\":\"Additional information\",\"level\":2}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"Use the \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/api#tag/services\",\"children\":\"Services endpoint\"}],\" in the \",[\"$\",\"$L14\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/reference/tailscale-api\",\"children\":\"Tailscale API\"}],\" to manage Services for your tailnet.\",\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/api#tag/services/GET/tailnet/%7Btailnet%7D/services\",\"children\":\"List all services\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/api#tag/services/GET/tailnet/%7Btailnet%7D/services/%7BserviceName%7D\",\"children\":\"Get a service\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/api#tag/services/PUT/tailnet/%7Btailnet%7D/services/%7BserviceName%7D\",\"children\":\"Update a service\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/api#tag/services/DELETE/tailnet/%7Btailnet%7D/services/%7BserviceName%7D\",\"children\":\"Delete a service\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/api#tag/services/GET/tailnet/%7Btailnet%7D/services/%7BserviceName%7D/devices\",\"children\":\"List devices hosting a service\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/api#tag/services/GET/tailnet/%7Btailnet%7D/services/%7BserviceName%7D/device/%7BdeviceId%7D/approved\",\"children\":\"Get approval status of service on a device\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/api#tag/services/POST/tailnet/%7Btailnet%7D/services/%7BserviceName%7D/device/%7BdeviceId%7D/approved\",\"children\":\"Update approval status of service on a device\"}]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"For more information about using the \",[\"$\",\"$L14\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/features/tsnet\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tsnet\"}]}],\" package and \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"Server.ListenService\"}],\" with Go programs, refer to \",[\"$\",\"$L14\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/reference/tsnet-server-api\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tsnet\"}],\" server\"]}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"For a complete example that uses \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"Server.ListenService\"}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"ServiceModeHTTP\"}],\" with Tailscale Services, refer to \",[\"$\",\"$L14\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/features/tsnet/how-to/register-service\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tsnet\"}],\" and Tailscale Services\"]}],\".\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]]}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"aside\",null,{\"className\":\"js-docHighlight col-span-10 h-full pb-8 md:col-span-8 md:col-start-4 xl:col-span-2 xl:col-start-auto\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sticky top-36 flex flex-col gap-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L1b\",null,{\"data\":[{\"id\":\"use-cases\",\"text\":\"Use cases\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"prerequisites\",\"text\":\"Prerequisites\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"get-started\",\"text\":\"Get started\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"step-1-define-a-tailscale-service\",\"text\":\"Step 1: Define a Tailscale Service\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"step-2-configure-a-service-host\",\"text\":\"Step 2: Configure a Service host\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"step-3-approve-a-service-host\",\"text\":\"Step 3: Approve a Service host\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"step-4-access-tailscale-services-from-other-devices\",\"text\":\"Step 4: Access Tailscale Services from other devices\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"common-scenarios\",\"text\":\"Common scenarios\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"drain-a-host\",\"text\":\"Drain a host\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"remove-a-host-configuration\",\"text\":\"Remove a host configuration\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"remove-an-endpoint\",\"text\":\"Remove an endpoint\",\"level\":4},{\"id\":\"remove-all-endpoint-mappings-for-a-service\",\"text\":\"Remove all endpoint mappings for a Service\",\"level\":4},{\"id\":\"remove-all-service-configurations\",\"text\":\"Remove all Service configurations\",\"level\":4},{\"id\":\"update-a-service-host-configuration\",\"text\":\"Update a Service host configuration\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"configure-a-service-host-using-a-configuration-file\",\"text\":\"Configure a Service host using a configuration file\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"set-up-automatic-approval\",\"text\":\"Set up automatic approval\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"validate-your-service\",\"text\":\"Validate your Service\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"configure-service-access\",\"text\":\"Configure Service access\",\"level\":4},{\"id\":\"use-access-control-tests\",\"text\":\"Use access control tests\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"check-availability\",\"text\":\"Check availability\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"reference\",\"text\":\"Reference\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"endpoint-types\",\"text\":\"Endpoint types\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"layer-7-endpoints-application-layer\",\"text\":\"Layer 7 endpoints (application layer)\",\"level\":4},{\"id\":\"layer-4-endpoints-transport-layer\",\"text\":\"Layer 4 endpoints (transport layer)\",\"level\":4},{\"id\":\"layer-3-endpoints-network-layer\",\"text\":\"Layer 3 endpoints (network layer)\",\"level\":4},{\"id\":\"service-states\",\"text\":\"Service states\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"limitations\",\"text\":\"Limitations\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"additional-information\",\"text\":\"Additional information\",\"level\":2}]}],null,[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sticky top-brand-12\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L1c\",null,{}]}]]}]}]]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"d:[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"content\":\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"theme-color\",\"content\":\"#fff\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"2\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"title\",\"3\",{\"children\":\"Tailscale Services · Tailscale Docs\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"4\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"Securely connect to and manage access to your internal resources using Tailscale Services.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"5\",{\"name\":\"robots\",\"content\":\"index, follow\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"6\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://tailscale.com/docs/features/tailscale-services\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"7\",{\"rel\":\"alternate\",\"type\":\"text/markdown\",\"href\":\"https://tailscale.com/docs/features/tailscale-services.md\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"property\":\"og:title\",\"content\":\"Tailscale Services · Tailscale Docs\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"9\",{\"property\":\"og:description\",\"content\":\"Securely connect to and manage access to your internal resources using Tailscale Services.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"10\",{\"property\":\"og:url\",\"content\":\"https://tailscale.com/features/tailscale-services\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"11\",{\"property\":\"og:site_name\",\"content\":\"Tailscale\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"12\",{\"property\":\"og:image\",\"content\":\"https://tailscale.com/files/images/og-image.png\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"13\",{\"property\":\"og:type\",\"content\":\"article\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"14\",{\"name\":\"twitter:card\",\"content\":\"summary_large_image\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"15\",{\"name\":\"twitter:creator\",\"content\":\"@tailscale\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"16\",{\"name\":\"twitter:title\",\"content\":\"Tailscale Services\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"17\",{\"name\":\"twitter:description\",\"content\":\"Securely connect to and manage access to your internal resources using Tailscale Services.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"18\",{\"name\":\"twitter:image\",\"content\":\"https://tailscale.com/files/images/og-image.png\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"19\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/favicon.png\",\"type\":\"image/png\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"20\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/favicon.svg\",\"type\":\"image/svg+xml\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"21\",{\"name\":\"next-size-adjust\"}]]\n6:null\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1d:I[74001,[\"34169\",\"static/chunks/34169-b6fa802ab0a73784.js\",\"72972\",\"static/chunks/72972-0a07a3915dc70b19.js\",\"95726\",\"static/chunks/95726-43e80890dd4575db.js\",\"99837\",\"static/chunks/99837-fee3a0400dacea0a.js\",\"41483\",\"static/chunks/41483-c8cbb1f45e3327c4.js\",\"63185\",\"static/chunks/app/layout-35c25c86fb791314.js\"],\"default\"]\n1e:I[72424,[\"34169\",\"static/chunks/34169-b6fa802ab0a73784.js\",\"72972\",\"static/chunks/72972-0a07a3915dc70b19.js\",\"95726\",\"static/chunks/95726-43e80890dd4575db.js\",\"99837\",\"static/chunks/99837-fee3a0400dacea0a.js\",\"41